            <ArticleTitle>Biphasic Zika Illness With Rash and Joint Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>ofx133</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/ofid/ofx133</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>During the current Zika virus (ZIKV) outbreak, acute symptomatic ZIKV infection in adults appears to be a mild-to-moderate, self-limited illness. We present a case of ZIKV rash illness that improved and then relapsed without repeat exposure to ZIKV. Clinicians should be alert for relapses in patients with ZIKV infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
